module contract;

// Fluent Bit input-chunk size queries — resource-projection vocabulary v1.
//
// Card W29-CORPUS-CONTRACTS. TWO TRUSTED ASSUMPTIONS about two upstream
// functions. This module verifies nothing: the C bodies are not analyzed by
// this loader, and a declaration is a premise. Any verdict that rests on it is
// a verdict RELATIVE TO these declarations, never a proof of the C
// implementation.
//
// Both bodies were read at Fluent Bit
// `66910c10a4d7eafa810b84229cf2dcf7b0f26f97` and are cited by line. The C
// declarations in force are `include/fluent-bit/flb_input_chunk.h:167-168`:
//
//     ssize_t flb_input_chunk_get_size(struct flb_input_chunk *ic);
//     ssize_t flb_input_chunk_get_real_size(struct flb_input_chunk *ic);
//
// `ssize_t` resolves to `long int` on the LP64 model the audited targets use,
// so `isize` is an admissible spelling of the result under the declared-ABI
// agreement gate (standing constraint 8); the parameter is one object-pointer
// level, spelled `ptr<mut, u8>` as every object pointer of this vocabulary is.
//
// ## `flb_input_chunk_get_size`, read from `src/flb_input_chunk.c:756-759`
//
//     ssize_t flb_input_chunk_get_size(struct flb_input_chunk *ic)
//     {
//         return cio_chunk_get_content_size(ic->chunk);
//     }
//
// That is the whole body. `cio_chunk_get_content_size`
// (`lib/chunkio/src/cio_chunk.c:315-334`) resets the chunk's own error field
// (`cio_error_reset`, `lib/chunkio/src/cio_error.c:56-59`, which is one store
// `ch->error_n = 0;`), reads the backend's length field on either storage arm
// (`mf->buf_len` or `cf->data_size`), and returns it — or `-1` on an
// unrecognized storage type. It allocates nothing, frees nothing, stores no
// pointer and retains nothing.
//
// ## `flb_input_chunk_get_real_size`, read from `src/flb_input_chunk.c:767-790`
//
//     ssize_t flb_input_chunk_get_real_size(struct flb_input_chunk *ic)
//
// Four callees, each read:
//
//   * `cio_chunk_get_real_size(ic->chunk)` (`:772`;
//     `lib/chunkio/src/cio_chunk.c:336-361`) — the same error-field reset and
//     field reads as its content-size sibling; on the filesystem arm with
//     `cf->fs_size == 0` it calls `cio_file_real_size`
//     (`lib/chunkio/src/cio_file.c:576-588`), which reads the file's size into
//     a local through `cio_file_native_get_size` and returns it. No custody
//     anywhere.
//   * `flb_input_chunk_get_size(ic)` (`:779`) — this module's own first
//     declaration.
//   * `flb_debug(...)` with `flb_input_chunk_get_name(ic)` in its argument
//     list (`:781-782`) — the logging vocabulary `fluent_bit/logging.qcore`
//     declares (all parameters borrowed) and the name accessor
//     `fluent_bit/input_chunk_name.qcore` declares (borrowed, result carries
//     no custody).
//   * `cio_meta_size(ic->chunk)` (`:786`; `lib/chunkio/src/cio_meta.c:75-89`)
//     — the memory arm reads `mf->meta_len`; the filesystem arm first calls
//     `cio_file_read_prepare` (`lib/chunkio/src/cio_file.c:505-508`), which is
//     one call `mmap_file(ctx, ch, 0)`: it (re)maps the chunk's OWN file into
//     the chunk's OWN state (`cf->map`). That is a mutation of `ic`'s object
//     graph whose result the chunk itself owns and releases; nothing is handed
//     to the caller and nothing of the caller's is released.
//
// The rest of the body is scalar arithmetic on locals (`:787`) and returns.
//
// ## Which mode is faithful
//
// Both bodies read fields, call read-only queries, and return a scalar. On
// every path the caller keeps exactly the obligations it had before the call:
// `resource_borrowed(ic)` states that, and it is the only v1 parameter mode
// with that caller-side effect (`owned` demands live custody, `consumed`
// transfers, `released` discharges, `out` creates custody at a destination,
// `stored` transfers under an owner and `removed` detaches from one). Writing
// into `ic`'s own fields — the error-field reset, the filesystem arm's remap —
// does not move custody, exactly as `input_chunk_write_header`'s writes
// through `chunk` did not (`fluent_bit/input_chunk_helpers.qcore`).
//
// The RESULT is a byte count (or a negative status), a value with no identity:
// `resource_return_none()`.
//
// Neither declaration says anything about `ic` being non-null — both bodies
// dereference it unconditionally, but `resource_borrowed` imposes NO non-null
// precondition, which is the weaker statement and deliberately so: a mode that
// demanded entry custody would delete the caller's failure paths. This is the
// same position `fluent_bit/input_chunk_name.qcore` records for the same
// receiver.
//
// ## Why these functions are declared although the analysed unit defines them
//
// Both are defined in `src/flb_input_chunk.c`, itself a unit of the pinned
// corpus, so this is the arrangement cards PROD-CONTRACTS, NEIGHBOURS,
// ADDRESS-OF-MEMBER-DESTROY-UNDECLARED and AOM-DESTROY-SIBLINGS already
// established: a declared contract ALWAYS wins over a W4-inferred summary, a
// disagreement is reported as a `SummaryConflict` diagnostic and never
// silently resolved (`crates/qcore-c-gateway/src/legacy_summary.rs`), and
// declaring a defined function does not stop the unit analysing that
// function's own body — it only fixes what its CALLERS may assume. Each
// function's own status is whatever its body earns, and this module does not
// move it.
//
// ## NOT CLAIMED, recorded rather than hidden
//
//   * **Nothing about the returned value's meaning.** `-1` on an unrecognized
//     storage type, `-1` from `flb_input_chunk_get_real_size` when the chunk
//     is empty (`:783`), a `0` from a failed `stat` inside
//     `cio_file_real_size` — all value semantics, outside a custody
//     projection.
//   * **Nothing about the filesystem arm's remap succeeding**, or about the
//     mapping it replaces. `mmap_file`'s failure returns an error status the
//     size query folds into `-1`; whether the chunk is left up or down is
//     chunk-residency state (`chunkio/chunk_residency.qcore` declares the
//     explicit residency entry points; this module declares nothing about
//     residency).
//   * **Nothing about retention.** Whether any other object holds `ic` or its
//     interior pointers is the unmodeled retention this corpus records as
//     B03/R13 and is not decided here.
//   * **`cio_chunk_get_content_size` itself remains UNDECLARED.** It is
//     called directly (not through this wrapper) at one refused site of the
//     corpus (`flb_input_chunk_map`), but its receiver there is the chained
//     actual `ic->chunk`, and a ChunkIO-side declaration is a different
//     library's module with its own reading; this card declares only the two
//     Fluent Bit wrappers it read the callers of. Named
//     `W29-CONTENT-SIZE-UNDECLARED`.

// --- the chunk's content size, as the input layer queries it ---------------
extern fn flb_input_chunk_get_size(ic: ptr<mut, u8>) -> isize
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(ic);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};

// --- the chunk's real (filesystem-inclusive) size ---------------------------
extern fn flb_input_chunk_get_real_size(ic: ptr<mut, u8>) -> isize
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(ic);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
